@OS_NAME@ @VERSION@ for the @MODEL_NAME@: SD card image
================================================================

pocket-ui is a game launcher with its own libretro frontend. This card (pocket-ui @VERSION@) starts it when the
handheld boots from it. This card does not flash anything to the handheld, and takes nothing off its internal storage.

@OS_NAME@ is built on ROCKNIX @ROCKNIX_TAG@ (https://rocknix.org): its kernel, system and emulators are
ROCKNIX's. pocket-ui is not made or endorsed by the ROCKNIX team; please report problems with this card to
pocket-ui (@ISSUES_URL@), not to ROCKNIX.


Before you start: your handheld needs one thing first
-----------------------------------------------------

A new @MODEL_NAME@ starts Android and can't start from a card. ROCKNIX fixes that with a small boot helper (its "ABL")
that goes into the handheld once, from Android, with root rights. This card does not flash it and does not carry it (ROCKNIX's
ABL comes without a stated licence and without source). If your handheld already starts ROCKNIX from a card, it has the
helper and it's set up: skip to Install.

If not, follow ROCKNIX's own guide for your model at https://rocknix.org. In short, from ROCKNIX's official image for this
family (ROCKNIX-SM8550, folder rocknix_abl on its first partition, README inside): back up the current helper and flash the
new one from Android, then restart while holding Volume Down to get its menu. There, pick "Set device model" and choose
your handheld, then "Switch boot mode", and start. This changes the handheld's bootloader, so read their guide first;
done wrong it can stop the handheld from starting, and it's at your own risk. pocket-ui never does this for you and never
changes the bootloader afterwards.


If you installed ROCKNIX onto the handheld's internal storage, this card won't take over: ROCKNIX looks for its partitions
by name, and the internal ones have the same names and win. The handheld starts your internal system as before and only
sees this card as a games card. Nothing is lost, but you won't get pocket-ui this way: add pocket-ui to your internal system
with its install package instead.


Install
-------

1. Write @IMAGE_NAME@.img.xz to a microSD card with balenaEtcher or Raspberry Pi
   Imager. Both read the .xz file directly. Everything on the card is erased. 8 GB or more.
   Use a spare card, not the one the handheld came with.
2. Put the card into the card slot of the switched-off handheld and switch it on.
3. The first start takes a few minutes and restarts once by itself while the card's storage is set up.
   Then pocket-ui's first-start setup opens: look, Wi-Fi, extras.


Add your games
--------------

Settings, Games, Add games shows the folder of each system. Turn on file sharing on that page and copy your games from your
computer over Wi-Fi.

Your computer can't write to the card's large STORAGE part without extra software, and Windows may ask to format it:
never say yes, press Cancel. Formatting would erase pocket-ui from the card.


If the screen stays black, switch off (hold Power for 10 seconds) and report it with the model.
To go back to what the handheld ran before, switch off and swap the card back.

This card contains no games and no console maker's BIOS files (the BIOS files in it are open replacements: DraStic's pair and ReGBA's). Add only games and BIOS files you own.
Remote access (SSH), file sharing and Syncthing are off. When you turn on Remote access or file
sharing in pocket-ui's Settings, it makes a password for this device and shows it on the screen.
(EmulationStation, ROCKNIX's menu, can also turn SSH on; it then uses ROCKNIX's standard root password
"rocknix" until you change it there.)
Updates come from pocket-ui (Settings, Updates). ROCKNIX's own updates would replace the system on this card
behind pocket-ui's back and flash the handheld's boot helper, so this card does not install them: the boot hook moves
any update pocket-ui did not check (from EmulationStation's menu, the network share "update" or copied
by hand) to /storage/.update-refused and starts as usual. Nothing there is deleted.


What is on the card
-------------------

FAT partition "ROCKNIX" (readable on any computer):
  KERNEL, KERNEL.md5         ROCKNIX @ROCKNIX_TAG@, unchanged (ROCKNIX-SM8550.aarch64-@ROCKNIX_TAG@.img.gz)
  SYSTEM, SYSTEM.md5         ROCKNIX @ROCKNIX_TAG@'s system, repacked without the files listed under
                             "Changes" below; everything else in it is unchanged
  post-flash.sh              boot hook: starts without the ROCKNIX logo
  mount-storage.sh           boot hook: puts pocket-ui's start entry in place once the storage has
                             grown; at every start, sets aside system updates pocket-ui did not check
  pocket-ui-info/            this file; SOURCE-OFFER.txt; pocket-ui-os.txt (name and version, shown
                             in Settings, About); pocket-ui's LICENSE and NOTICE.md;
                             licences/ (the Rust crates' licence texts and the fonts' OFL; /storage/pocket-ui/licences
                             links here); rocknix-licenses/ (ROCKNIX's
                             LICENSE.md and licenses folder at tag @ROCKNIX_TAG@); firmware-licences/
                             (the terms of the firmware files inside SYSTEM)

Partition "STORAGE" (grows to fill the card at the first start):
  pocket-ui/                 pocket-ui, pocket-core and pocket-splash (the boot screen) @VERSION@, the launcher
  .pocket-seed/              the start entry for pocket-ui and the boot screen's unit (moved to
                             .config/system.d at the second start), and a script ROCKNIX runs once
                             at the first start: device name "pocket-ui", ROCKNIX's update check off

Changes from the ROCKNIX image: ROCKNIX's rocknix_abl folder is left off, and the files above were added (the hooks, pocket-ui-info/, pocket-ui/).
Removed from SYSTEM:
  - ROCKNIX's ABL (usr/share/bootloader/rocknix_abl): no stated licence and no source, and this card never flashes it.
  - firmware for handhelds this image isn't for: the AYANEO Pocket family and the AYN Thor (qcom/sm8550/ayaneo,
    qcom/sm8550/ayn/thor; from ROCKNIX's extra-firmware, which states no licence).
  - the Kickstart relocation tables (kick*.RTB) of Amiberry's WHDLoad booter, loose and inside its
    boot-data.zip (the rest of that archive is unchanged). They come from SKick
    (aminet.net, util/boot/skick346.lha), whose licence allows passing them on only inside that unchanged
    archive. Amiga games run with the standard emulator as before; for WHDLoad games in Amiberry,
    copy the .RTB files from that archive to /storage/.config/amiberry/whdboot/save-data/Kickstarts.
  - the DOOM shareware game data (usr/share/idtech/doom.tar.gz), so the card holds no games; its
    shareware terms also ask for the complete, unchanged shareware package.
The partition table and KERNEL are unchanged. ROCKNIX's own interface, EmulationStation, stays on
the card and takes over if pocket-ui cannot start.


Licences
--------

This image may be shared free of charge, for non-commercial use only. Do not sell it, and do not
bundle it with hardware you sell. Reasons: ROCKNIX includes components licensed for non-commercial use
only (for example the libretro cores snes9x, genesis_plus_gx, picodrive and fbneo), and its artwork is
licensed CC BY-NC-SA 4.0.

ROCKNIX (KERNEL, SYSTEM)
  Copyright ROCKNIX (https://github.com/ROCKNIX). ROCKNIX is a fork of JELOS
  (https://github.com/JustEnoughLinuxOS/distribution); credit to the JELOS team.
  The ROCKNIX team's own software and scripts: GNU GPL version 2. Every bundled component keeps its own
  licence: see pocket-ui-info/rocknix-licenses/ (ROCKNIX's LICENSE.md and licenses folder) and each
  package's PKG_LICENSE in ROCKNIX's source.
  ROCKNIX branding and images (logos, splash artwork, EmulationStation themes inside SYSTEM):
  CC BY-NC-SA 4.0, https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/ . They are included unchanged
  inside SYSTEM; this image does not use them as its own branding.

Firmware inside SYSTEM (usr/lib/kernel-overlays/base/lib/firmware): Qualcomm Wi-Fi, Bluetooth and graphics firmware from
  linux-firmware 20260309 and the wireless regulatory database from wireless-regdb 2026.05.30, all unchanged, under the
  terms in pocket-ui-info/firmware-licences/. The rest comes from ROCKNIX's extra-firmware repository, which states no
  licence (its package says "proprietary"): the sound and battery firmware of these handhelds (qcom/sm8550/ayn), which they
  can't work without, and a few more files. It is passed on unchanged, as ROCKNIX does, and we remove it on request of
  whoever holds the rights. README.txt in that folder lists every file and where it comes from.

Linux kernel (KERNEL): GNU GPL version 2. The device trees are ROCKNIX's, unchanged, inside KERNEL.

DraStic (usr/config/drastic in SYSTEM): the Nintendo DS emulator DraStic by Exophase (https://www.drastic-ds.com/) is
  closed-source software. It is passed on unchanged, as ROCKNIX does, on the basis of the author's 2017 forum
  statement that there is "no real harm" in distributing it (usr/config/drastic/LICENSE.pdf, and ROCKNIX's
  pocket-ui-info/rocknix-licenses/licenses/DRASTIC.pdf). That is a tolerance, not a formal licence, and no source
  code for it exists. Credit: Exophase. We remove it from the image on request of the author.
  Its BIOS replacement (drastic_bios_arm7.bin, drastic_bios_arm9.bin) is open: Gilead Kutnick, BSD licence, text in
  usr/config/drastic/system/drastic_bios_readme.txt.

pocket-ui and pocket-core
  GNU GPL version 2 or later (pocket-ui-info/LICENSE).
  Source: @POCKET_UI_SOURCE@.
  Third-party credits (fonts, Rust crates and other parts, each under its own licence) are in
  NOTICE.md: pocket-ui-info/NOTICE.md on this card, and in the repository. The licence texts of the Rust crates
  and of the fonts (SIL Open Font License) are in pocket-ui-info/licences/.


Source code
-----------

pocket-ui's source and the scripts that build this image are next to the image on @RELEASE_URL@
(pocket-ui-@VERSION@-source.tar.gz); the rest of the source is public at the links below. For at least three
years from the release of this image, anyone can ask for the complete corresponding source code of the GNU GPL
and LGPL software on this card, for no charge beyond the cost of providing it: open an issue at the project's
GitHub page. See pocket-ui-info/SOURCE-OFFER.txt.

ROCKNIX @ROCKNIX_TAG@, including the kernel and its patches:
  https://github.com/ROCKNIX/distribution/tree/@ROCKNIX_TAG@
  tag @ROCKNIX_TAG@, commit @ROCKNIX_COMMIT@
pocket-ui, pocket-core and the scripts that make this image: @POCKET_UI_SOURCE@
  (scripts/make-image-family.sh --family SM8550 rebuilds this image from the ROCKNIX release above;
  scripts/check-image-family.sh checks it).
